<title>BELGIUM: EU approves two gene-modified rapeseed varieties.</title>
<headline>EU approves two gene-modified rapeseed varieties.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission on Friday approved the release of two herbicide resistant, genetically modified rapeseed varieties, EU Commission officials said.  </p>
<p>The varieties were developed by Belgium-based biotech company Plant Genetic Systems.</p>
<p>A Commission official said approval was given after the company agreed to voluntary labelling of the products.</p>
<p>Labelling is not compulsory for the 11 genetically modified products that are being examined by the European Commission.</p>
<p>Approval follows a French government request to the Commission in July 1995.</p>
<p>-Brussels newsroom +322 287 6830</p>
</text>
